{"name":"Arctic Paradise","hex":"#b8dff8","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"arctic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Arctic."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Arctic."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arctic"},{"term":"paradise","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The place where sanctified souls are believed to live after death.","A very pleasant place, such as a place full of lush vegetation."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Paradise (“Heaven”).","Alternative letter-case form of Paradise (“the Garden of Eden”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/paradise"}],"entries":[{"title":"Arctic","blocks":[{"text":"The Arctic is the polar region of Earth that surrounds the North Pole, lying north of the Arctic Circle. The Arctic region, from the IERS Reference Meridian travelling east, consists of parts of northern Norway, northernmost Sweden, northern Finland, Russia, the United States (Alaska), Canada, Danish Realm (Greenland), and northern Iceland, along with the Arctic Ocean and adjacent seas."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Arctic_%28orthographic_projection_with_highlights%29.svg/330px-Arctic_%28orthographic_projection_with_highlights%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arctic","wikidata":"Q25322"},{"title":"Paradise","blocks":[{"text":"In religion and folklore, paradise is a place of everlasting happiness, delight, and bliss. Paradisiacal notions are often laden with pastoral imagery, and may be cosmogonical, eschatological, or both, often contrasted with the miseries of human civilization: in paradise there is only peace, prosperity, and happiness. Paradise is a place of contentment, a land of luxury and fulfillment containing ever-lasting bliss and delight. Paradise is often described as a \"higher place\", the holiest place, in contrast to this world, or underworlds such as hell."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Angelico%2C_giudizio_universale_01.jpg/330px-Angelico%2C_giudizio_universale_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paradise","wikidata":"Q3363340"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Arctica_surface.jpg/500px-Arctica_surface.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Arctica_surface.jpg/500px-Arctica_surface.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AArctica_surface.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Sunny_Skies_over_the_Arctic_in_Late_June_2010.jpg/500px-Sunny_Skies_over_the_Arctic_in_Late_June_2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Sunny_Skies_over_the_Arctic_in_Late_June_2010.jpg/1280px-Sunny_Skies_over_the_Arctic_in_Late_June_2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Sunny_Skies_over_the_Arctic_in_Late_June_2010.jpg/500px-Sunny_Skies_over_the_Arctic_in_Late_June_2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASunny_Skies_over_the_Arctic_in_Late_June_2010.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Aerial_photograph_Greenland_2023-10-14-3.jpg/500px-Aerial_photograph_Greenland_2023-10-14-3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/